(The proposed $5.8B take-private of Option Care Health, Inc. by Onyx Bidco LLC combines a $3.15B debt package with $2.873B in equity commitments, including a) Tj
T* ($1.4B minority co-investment by wholesale pharmaceutical distributor McKesson Corporation \(~48.725% of equity\) alongside Clayton, Dubilier & Rice Fund XII. The) Tj
T* (transaction contains no contractual financing condition and designates the Target an express third-party beneficiary entitled to seek specific performance of the equity) Tj
T* (commitments. However, the transaction architecture exhibits critical exposure at the intersection of syndicate structure and regulatory standards: equity commitments) Tj
T* (and the $291.93M Parent Termination Fee limited guarantees are several and not joint, leaving Option Care without recourse against the non-defaulting sponsor if) Tj
T* (either party fails to fund. Furthermore, while Parent is subject to a heightened 'best efforts' obligation for state healthcare and pharmacy licensing across Target's 86) Tj
T* (pharmacies and 187 ambulatory infusion suites, antitrust clearance under the HSR Act is governed solely by a mutual 'reasonable best efforts' standard. Because) Tj
T* (Option Care sourced 68% of its supplies from four wholesale distributors in 2025 and 57% from three in H1 2026, combining McKesson's distribution scale with) Tj
T* (Target's downstream network creates vertical foreclosure scrutiny that the Buyer Consortium is not contractually bound to resolve through burdensome divestitures) Tj
T* (under a reasonable best efforts threshold prior to the October 5, 2027 outside date.) Tj
